<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dál gCais</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dal Cais, Dalcassians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dál gCais were an Irish dynasty of north Munster, with lands in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-clare">County Clare</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a>. Originally minor, they rose in the 10th century under Mathgamain and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru</a>, who took Norse Limerick and Cashel and became high king of Ireland. Their descendants, the O'Briens, ruled Thomond until 1543.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dal-cais.jpg" alt="Dál gCais" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Myself · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sword_of_Nuada.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
